    "Simulation is active. ThermalPilot does not control heating.": "Simulatie actief. ThermalPilot regelt de verwarming niet.",
    "Observation and learning only; no thermostat control.": "Alleen waarneming en leren; geen regeling.",
    "ThermalPilot controls thermostat targets.": "ThermalPilot regelt thermostaatdoelen.",
    "Seasonal fallback temperatures are used.": "Seizoensfallbacktemperaturen gebruikt.",
    "Scheduled targets remain simulated; season transitions can change thermostat targets.": "Plan blijft simulatie; seizoenen kunnen echte doelen wijzigen.",
    "Live thermostat control is not enabled.": "Werkelijke regeling niet ingeschakeld.",
    "Target changes include the shared start/stop offsets. The temperature forecast models the planned heating period; actual valve and heat-pump delays must be checked against observations.": "Start/stopverschuivingen inbegrepen. Controleer werkelijke klep- en pompvertragingen.",
    "These forecasts were saved 1, 3 or 6 hours before the measurements. Later readings do not change them. Lower error is better; compare it with simply predicting no temperature change. Different heating, computers and other heat sources can affect the result.": "Voorspellingen 1, 3 of 6 uur eerder opgeslagen, later onveranderd. Kleinere afwijking beter; vergelijk met constante temperatuur. Andere warmte beïnvloedt resultaat.",
    "Compare recorded temperatures with forecasts saved hours earlier. The accuracy cards also compare against predicting no temperature change. Forecasts assume the proposed heating plan; actual heating may differ, especially during simulation.": "Vergelijk met eerder opgeslagen voorspellingen en constante temperatuur. Echte verwarming kan afwijken, vooral tijdens simulatie.",
    "Forecasts are compared with measurements within five minutes of their due time. “Similar heating” means observed demand matched the forecast for at least 90% of observations, with no large recording gaps. These counts give context, not a guarantee of accuracy.": "Meting binnen vijf minuten. Vergelijkbare verwarming: ≥90% overeenkomst zonder grote gaten. Aantallen garanderen geen nauwkeurigheid.",
    "Each row shows the latest observation within its 15-minute interval, not an average. Suggested thermostat target is the setting ThermalPilot would apply, not a room-temperature forecast. Table shows up to 288 intervals. Original observations remain stored internally. Short chart views use 15-minute time labels; longer views use wider intervals.": "Laatste waarneming per 15 minuten, geen gemiddelde. Doel is thermostaatinstelling, geen voorspelling. Maximaal 288 intervallen; origineel blijft bewaard.",
    "Suggested On means the boosted target window, including valve timing offsets. Relay On means observed demand; it does not guarantee heat flow.": "Voorgesteld Aan is verhoogd doel met klepverschuiving. Relais Aan toont vraag, geen gegarandeerde warmte.",
    ", without heating, remaining slab warmth or appliance heat. Lower temperature loss means slower modeled cooling. This is a model estimate, not measured energy efficiency or an insulation rating.": ", zonder verwarming, restwarmte of apparaten. Lager verlies is tragere modelafkoeling; geen energie- of isolatiebeoordeling.",
    "Cooling-speed bands are provisional: under 1 h, 1–2 h, 2–4 h, 4–8 h, and 8 h or longer per 1°C drop. For a selected house type, badges instead compare with that type: under 0.5×, 0.5–0.8×, 0.8–1.25×, 1.25–2×, and at least 2× its reference cooling time. Initial rooms share starting estimates and remain unrated. Comparisons become more useful as their heat-loss parameters adapt to observations. Wind, ventilation, sensor placement and unmeasured heat sources can affect the estimates. The listed time describes this reference test, not how long heating can safely remain off in your home.": "Beginmodellen gelijk. Wind, ventilatie, sensoren en andere warmte beïnvloeden vergelijking. Referentietijd is geen veilige uitschakelduur.",
    "Learned parameters and season aggregates are retained when old observations are compacted.": "Geleerde parameters en seizoenstotalen blijven bij comprimeren.",
    "Open a Home Assistant dashboard once, then return here to load embedded history cards.": "Open Home Assistant-dashboard en keer terug om geschiedenis te laden.",
    "Water-based systems only: raise the thermostat target this many minutes before the planned heat-delivery session, allowing slow valves to open. Electric and air distribution ignore this setting and use no advance offset.": "Alleen water: vooraf verhogen voor trage kleppen. Elektra/lucht negeren verschuiving.",
    "Water-based systems only: lower the thermostat target this many minutes before the planned heat-delivery session ends, allowing valves to close. Electric and air distribution ignore this setting and use no closing offset.": "Alleen water: eerder verlagen voor sluitende kleppen. Elektra/lucht negeren verschuiving.",
    "What produces heat for your house. Select air-to-water for your water floor system supplied by an air-source heat pump. Gas, oil, wood and district heating need their own fuel-cost logic; choosing a house detail does not yet enable a different controller or reset learned room data.": "Warmtebron van huis. Brandstoffen krijgen geen eigen kostenregeling; kamerdata behouden.",
    "How heat reaches rooms: circulating water in floors or radiators, electric floor/ceiling/panels, or warm air. Mixed means different rooms use different systems. Water distribution can optionally use a heating-water sensor and uses valve timing. Electric and warm-air distribution ignore those inputs and learn response from observed thermostat demand. Mixed and Other retain water requirements until room overrides are supported.": "Water gebruikt kleptijden en optionele sensor. Elektra/lucht leren van vraag. Gemengd behoudt waterinstellingen.",
    "The construction around floor heating, which affects how slowly heat is stored and released. Concrete slab describes your heated floor. Choose Not applicable if there is no floor heating. This does not change your configured response lag or erase learned parameters.": "Vloermateriaal beïnvloedt opslag. Geen vloerverwarming: Niet van toepassing. Wijzigt geen vertraging of model.",
    "The structure below your home: slab on ground, crawl space or basement. A heated concrete floor can be above a basement, so this is separate from Heated floor. Choose Unknown if unsure. This descriptive setting does not reset observation history or learned models.": "Fundering apart van verwarmde vloer. Kies Onbekend bij twijfel. Modellen en historie blijven.",
    "Sunlight through large windows, especially south-facing windows, can warm a room. No additional physical solar heating system is needed. Select the main direction of those windows to enable solar estimates, or Solar heating off to turn them off. Home Assistant’s location determines seasonal sun elevation and azimuth; cloud conditions come from your weather source. The effect starts at zero and learns gradually. Missing sunlight data assumes no solar warmth; room temperature limits still apply.": "Zon door grote ramen, geen zonne-installatie nodig. Richting, locatie en wolken geven zonbijdrage, geleerd vanaf nul. Ontbrekende data: geen zonwarmte; temperatuurgrenzen gelden.",
    "Clear means the windows receive direct sunlight without major obstructions. Choose Partly shaded for some trees, buildings or overhangs, or Mostly shaded when sunlight is usually blocked. Forecasts use a more cautious solar allowance: partly shaded uses 65% and mostly shaded 30% of the clear allowance. Actual room warming is still learned from observations; no solar heat is assumed before learning. Seasonal leaf cover and changing shading can still affect accuracy.": "Vrij, deels of veel schaduw: 100%, 65% of 30% zonbijdrage in voorspelling. Werkelijke warmte geleerd; schaduw kan veranderen.",
    "Optional local wind sensor, for example sensor.netatmo_tuuli_ms using m/s. Valid readings are averaged over the last 30 minutes. ThermalPilot learns a separate wind effect only after enough varied observations; no fixed wind penalty is assumed. Missing, invalid or unchanged-for-two-hours readings are ignored, and normal temperature-based planning and heating continue. Fresh wind correction gradually returns to typical conditions in forecasts further ahead. A stable calm reading may also be ignored conservatively. Units are detected automatically.": "Optionele wind, automatische eenheden, 30-minuutsgemiddelde. Effect geleerd uit gevarieerde data. Ontbrekend, ongeldig of 2 uur onveranderd genegeerd; normale verwarming blijft. Verre voorspelling keert naar typische wind.",
    "Emergency lower temperature limit shared by all rooms. Each room’s own target is the normal comfort goal. ThermalPilot prioritizes avoiding this limit even when electricity is expensive; this value is not the idle thermostat target.": "Absolute ondergrens, geen rustdoel. Kamerdoel is comfort; grens ook bij dure uren beschermd.",
    "Upper temperature limit shared by all rooms. Extra heating and heat storage must stay within this limit.": "Bovengrens voor alle kamers; extra warmte mag niet erboven.",
    "Optional sensor with forecast timestamp/value entries, such as Nordpool Predict FI. Only relative expensive/cheap patterns after confirmed prices are used, so no forecast price unit or additional costs are required. The Source price unit setting applies only to the confirmed total-price sensor. An expensive upcoming period can increase the heat reserve at the end of the known-price plan. Forecast prices are not compared directly with your total prices, used as confirmed prices or used to execute future heating commands. Missing forecasts keep normal planning. Confirmed prices always determine the executable schedule.": "Optionele relatieve prijstrend na bevestigde prijzen. Geen eenheid of extra kosten nodig. Kan reserve verhogen, nooit bevestigd prijsgegeven of direct toekomstig commando. Ontbrekend: normaal plan.",
    "Notify in Home Assistant when a room temperature sensor stays unchanged or unavailable for this many hours. A stable room can also have an unchanged reading, so the warning asks you to check the sensor. ThermalPilot sends at most one sensor notification per calendar day. Monitoring runs while ThermalPilot is active; long monitoring gaps restart the timer.": "Waarschuw na deze tijd zonder nieuwe kamertemperatuur.",
    "Summer fallback always applies from 15.5. through 30.9. Outside those dates, it also applies when the day’s lowest forecast temperature is equal to or above this value. For example, a setting of 6°C means the daily minimum must be at least 6°C for ThermalPilot to use summer fallback temperatures. Lower readings already observed that day are included. If a full-day forecast is unavailable outside the summer dates, winter fallback is used.": "Zomerfallback 15.5.–30.9., anders als volledige dagminimum boven grens. Geen voorspelling activeert geen zomer buiten die data.",
    "Negative values reduce estimated heat loss while the fireplace is active; −20% means a 20% reduction.": "Negatief verlaagt warmteverlies bij actieve haard; −20% is 20% minder.",
    "Prefer a sensor that includes electricity prices and additional costs, such as VAT, transfer tariffs, electricity tax and retailer margin. A variable electricity-price sensor without these costs also works. If transfer tariffs differ between day and night, including them helps ThermalPilot choose the cheapest heating hours; omitting them can shift heating to hours that are less economical overall. Select a source containing today/tomorrow or timestamped raw_today/raw_tomorrow price lists, and choose the matching source price unit.": "Voorkeur voor totale prijs met belasting, netkosten en marge. Variabel prijsdeel alleen werkt ook; ontbrekende dag/nachtnetkosten kunnen urenkeuze verslechteren. Gebruik today/tomorrow of gedateerde raw_today/raw_tomorrow met passende eenheid.",
    "Hourly average uses fixed hourly averages of the source prices. 15 minutes plans using quarter-hour intervals. Flexible builds heating sessions in 15-minute steps, allowing runs such as 60 or 75 minutes while respecting the minimum flexible heating run.": "Uurgemiddelde, 15-minuutinterval of flexibel in stappen van 15 min met minimumduur.",
    "The shortest planned heating session in flexible scheduling mode. Longer sessions can be chosen in 15-minute steps. This setting applies to flexible runs; valve opening and closing offsets are applied separately.": "Kortste flexibele sessie; langer in stappen van 15 min.",
    "Initial estimate of how slowly heat input affects room temperature and how long its effect persists. Concrete slabs often need a longer delay, but lightweight floors, radiators, electric heaters and air systems also have a response time. Use a shorter value for faster systems. This remains relevant to every distribution; it is separate from valve opening or closing time.": "Beginschatting van traagheid en restwarmte; model leert echte reactie.",
    "The warm outdoor endpoint of the initial heating-hours curve. At this temperature or warmer, the starting model assumes the lower daily heating need. This curve seeds the model before enough real heating and cooling observations are available.": "Warm beginpunt van dagelijkse warmtevraag; echte respons geleerd.",
    "The cold outdoor endpoint of the initial heating-hours curve. At this temperature or colder, the starting model assumes the higher daily heating need. Set it below the warm endpoint. Actual room response is learned from observations.": "Koud beginpunt, lager dan warm punt; echte respons geleerd.",
    "Allows real thermostat setpoint changes when ThermalPilot changes between Active and Passive. Active applies each room’s target temperature; Passive applies the seasonal fallback: the shared summer setpoint or each room’s normal target in winter. These commands can occur even with simulation enabled. This does not enable live heating schedule control.": "Echte seizoenswisselingen ook tijdens simulatie. Actief: kamerdoel; passief: zomer/winterfallback. Geen schemaregeling.",
    "The thermostat target used for all configured rooms while ThermalPilot is Passive, if real Active/Passive season setpoint control is enabled. A low summer target normally prevents heating without switching off the thermostats.": "Gedeeld zomerdoel in passief met seizoensregeling. Laag doel voorkomt meestal warmte zonder thermostaten uit te schakelen.",
    "Degrees added to each room’s target temperature during a suggested heating window. For example, a 20 °C target with a 1.5 °C boost suggests a 21.5 °C thermostat setpoint to store heat. Scheduled targets remain simulated in this version.": "Graden boven kamerdoel om warmte op te slaan, bv. 20 + 1,5 = 21,5°C.",
    "Negative values temporarily lower the thermostat target during expensive electricity hours. After a planned heating session, ThermalPilot first restores the room’s normal target. It then chooses reduction only when predicted stored warmth can avoid thermostat heating while supporting room comfort. For example, −1°C allows a 20°C target to be reduced to 19°C during selected costly hours. The reduced target never goes below Minimum allowed temperature. Normal target is restored when reduction is no longer useful; a new planned heating session uses the boosted target. Duration is chosen by the plan, not a fixed number of hours.": "Negatieve verlaging alleen in dure uren bij voldoende opgeslagen warmte. Eerst normaal na sessie, nooit onder minimum. Herstelt als niet nuttig; duur door plan.",
    "Select the measured supply-water temperature. A temperature sensor uses its state; a climate entity uses its current_temperature attribute. This is the measured water temperature, not the thermostat’s target. Optional for water-based systems. A valid reading adjusts the estimated heating output. Without it, planning and learning continue from observed thermostat demand, without a water-temperature adjustment. Missing readings do not force fallback targets.": "Optioneel gemeten toevoerwater; climate gebruikt current_temperature, niet doel. Corrigeert vermogen. Ontbreken stopt leren/planning niet en forceert geen fallback.",
    "Simulation calculates heating suggestions without applying scheduled targets. Disable simulation and confirm to enable real thermostat control. If another automation controls these thermostats, disable it first. Observation and learning continue in both modes.": "Simulatie past geen schemadoelen toe. Uit en bevestigen voor echte regeling; schakel andere betrokken automatisering uit als die bestaat. Leren in beide modi.",
    "Choose the interface language. Room and entity names remain unchanged. Save settings to keep the choice. Embedded history cards follow this choice where supported by Home Assistant.": "Kies taal en sla op. Kamer-/entiteitsnamen blijven. Ingebedde historie volgt waar ondersteund.",
    "All room timelines share the price chart’s time axis.${zones.length?' Zone rows show recorded heating and cooling only; off and standby periods stay empty. Plan adds suggested heating only for tariff-optimized zones.':''} Teal shows the suggested thermostat boost window; amber shows observed heating demand. ": "Gedeelde tijdas. Turkoois: verhoging; oranje: waargenomen vraag. ",
    "The selected period controls past history. Today and tomorrow are included when prices are published. Recorded activity is shown before now; future suggestions follow the current plan. Price gaps stay empty. ": "Periode bepaalt historie; vandaag/morgen bij prijzen. Vóór nu waarnemingen; erna huidige plan. Prijsgaten leeg. ",
    "Times align to 15-minute boundaries; wider views show fewer labels. Hover, focus or tap a price bar or heating period for details.": "15-minuutgrenzen; lange weergaven minder labels. Aanwijzen, focussen of tikken voor details.",
    "This measures initial data collection, not model trustworthiness. Continue validating forecasts and heating suggestions before enabling live control. Learning continues after initial data collection.": "Beginverzameling is geen betrouwbaarheid. Valideer voorstellen vóór echte regeling; leren gaat door.",
    "History collection and learning paused because outdoor temperature is unavailable. Existing model parameters are retained.": "Historie en leren gepauzeerd zonder buitentemperatuur. Model blijft.",
    "No weather forecast: current outdoor temperature is held constant.": "Geen weersvoorspelling; huidige buitentemperatuur constant gehouden.",
    "Live control awaits confirmation. Enable simulation, save, then disable it and confirm to activate thermostat control.": "Regeling wacht op bevestiging. Simulatie aan, opslaan, dan uit en bevestigen.",
    "Waiting for enough heating and idle observations to estimate the remaining time.": "Wachten op meer verwarmings- en rustwaarnemingen voor tijdschatting.",
    "A door/window contact sensor can monitor the fireplace damper position. Select the sensor state that means the fireplace is in use. For a damper contact sensor, Open normally means active and Closed means inactive. Door/window labels are converted to Home Assistant’s underlying on/off values. Other sensors show their declared options, current valid state and any saved value. A contact state indicates the damper position; it does not prove that a fire is burning.": "Deur-/raamcontact op haardklep: Open meestal actief, Gesloten niet. Opgeslagen als on/off. Andere sensoren tonen opties. Klepstand bewijst geen brandend vuur.",
